["er.request/1",{"definition_version":1,"fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"intent":{"causation":null,"command_id":"cmd-child-6187762f00bd37949563fd6b426ed35554be3c210a86ec0e3f09cdf8aac2f71b","command_type":"aep.entity.create/v1","correlation_id":"protocol-artifact-new","execution_id":null,"expected_revision":null,"payload":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"# Story: a recorded production history is validated against the specification (later milestone)\n\n## Outcome\n\nAn operator converts recorded command/response logs, such as an Eventlog stream, into\n`ess-history/1` through a declared adapter. `check-history` then judges the recorded history. A\nfield the log does not carry is reported as a coverage gap and never guessed. Precedents: AWS P +\nPObserve (post-hoc validation of structured service logs) and TLA+ trace validation (SEFM 2024,\narXiv 2404.16075).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A recorded history from the billing target with `LostUpdate` active is a violation. The same run\n  without the fault passes.\n- A log missing return instants is refused, with the missing field named per operation.\n\n## Scope\n\nAn adapter module beside the history format, and the `check-history` input path.\n","owner":"ess","status":"draft","tags":["later-milestone"],"title":"A recorded production history is validated against the specification"},"entity_type":"aep.story/v1","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/recorded-history-validation"},"target":null,"task":null},"result":{"affected":["ent-96d34f36e8782e7dc1a9ad245bf4353c@1"],"audit":["aud-0bc8722953092e5817ffb272ec0d3d0f"],"command_id":"cmd-child-6187762f00bd37949563fd6b426ed35554be3c210a86ec0e3f09cdf8aac2f71b","consistency":"seq-000000000000","events":["evt-0bc875295309337117ffb372ec0d3ec2"],"outcome":"accepted"}},"lifecycle_state":"recorded"}},"kind":"create","recording":{"actor":"human:timo","causation":"cmd-child-6187762f00bd37949563fd6b426ed35554be3c210a86ec0e3f09cdf8aac2f71b","correlation":"protocol-artifact-n